  "rationale": "Multiple direct-match hypertension PRS are present (e.g., PGS000706, PGS001320, PGS001838, PGS002047, PGS004234, PGS004236, PGS004934, etc.). Among these, PGS004236 is best supported in the provided context because it is explicitly aligned to hypertension (trait_efo/phenotyping_reported both hypertension) and comes from a disease-focused, multi-ethnic hypertension study (Nat Commun: “A multi-ethnic polygenic risk score is associated with hypertension prevalence and progression throughout adulthood.”), rather than a pan-trait/portability framework. It also reports strong full-model discrimination (AUROC 0.764 with CI) and a substantial effect size (OR 2.1, CI 1.99–2.21), supporting meaningful PRS signal. The main limitation is that the reported AUROC appears to be full-model (covariates include age, BMI, smoking, race/ethnic background, PCs), and no explicit PRS-only AUROC/R2 is provided, reducing cross-model comparability and keeping confidence below High despite strong endpoint fidelity and study design."
}

