  "rationale": "Direct-match hypertension candidates are present (e.g., PGS000706, PGS000957/PGS000958, PGS001320, PGS001838, PGS002047, PGS004234, PGS004236, PGS004934, etc.). Among these, PGS004236 is the best-supported based on (1) strong phenotype alignment (trait_efo=hypertension; phenotyping_reported=prevalent hypertension), (2) favorable method structure per provided domain guidance (PRSsum; not a sparse pan-trait UKB framework score), (3) comparatively strong reported full-model discrimination with basic-to-moderate epidemiologic covariates (AUROC=0.764 with age/age^2, BMI, smoking, ancestry PCs, etc.), and (4) supportive effect-size evidence (OR=2.1). Key limitation: no explicit PRS-only (covariate-free) discrimination metric is reported, and the AUROC/OR are from a covariate-adjusted model, so the standalone PRS contribution cannot be cleanly compared across candidates; therefore confidence is moderate rather than high."
