{
  "outcome": "DIRECT_HIGH_QUALITY",
  "best_model_id": "PGS000422",
  "confidence": "Moderate",
  "rationale": "Multiple direct-match melanoma PRSs are present (e.g., PGS000079, PGS000118, PGS000732, PGS000743, PGS000766, PGS001304, PGS002246/PGS002247, and the PRSweb ‘Melanomas of skin (dx or hx)’ series PGS000408–PGS000432). Among those with the cleanest endpoint alignment for generic melanoma risk and comparable reported metrics, PGS000422 stands out with a direct melanoma EFO and phenotype (‘Melanomas of skin, dx or hx’), European development/evaluation, and the strongest full-model discrimination within this coherent PRSweb melanoma cluster (AUROC 0.615 with reported R² 0.0332 and OR 1.539). Competing melanoma-labeled scores either have weaker reported discrimination in this context (e.g., PGS000079 full-model AUROC 0.652 but without a PRS-only metric; PGS000118 AUROC 0.61; PGS000732 AUROC 0.579; PGS002246/002247 AUROC ~0.688–0.691 but smaller validation n=4,765 and no PRS-only metric), are endpoint-restricted (familial melanoma PGS000813; second primary melanoma PGS003412; childhood cancer survivors PGS005208), or are pan-trait/framework-style (snpnet PGS001304) which domain guidance cautions may underperform disease-focused or coherent disease-endpoint families. Main limitation: across candidates, reported AUROCs are largely full-model and covariate-dependent (no clear PRS-only AUROC/R² for most), so the ranking relies on within-family comparability and available effect-size/metric fields rather than definitive PRS-only performance."
}

{"outcome":"DIRECT_SUB_OPTIMAL","best_model_id":"PGS005262","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"Direct-match candidates are present for the target trait nodular goiter, including (i) nontoxic multinodular goiter models (PGS001814, PGS002022) and (ii) benign nodular goiter models (PGS005261–PGS005263). Models contrasting thyroid carcinoma vs benign nodular goiter (PGS005273–PGS005274) are less directly aligned because the endpoint is a case-control contrast rather than nodular goiter status alone.

Among the direct nodular-goiter-status candidates, PGS005262 is preferred because it is phenotype-aligned (trait_reported/trait_efo indicate benign nodular goiter; phenotyping_reported is the same concept despite spelling noise) and uses a genome-wide Bayesian continuous shrinkage method (PRSCS) with very large variant count (~1.1M), which domain guidance treats as a strong structural signal. It also reports stronger effect-size evidence (OR per SD ~1.41) than the sibling PGS005263 (OR ~1.36) and much stronger than PGS005261 (OR ~1.05) from the same study family.

However, the recommendation remains sub-optimal because performance evidence is limited/comparability-unclear: the only AUROC shown is a full-model AUROC (not PRS-only), covariates are listed as Unknown for these models, and the publication is a preprint; additionally, the nontoxic multinodular goiter options come from a UKB portability framework study and report only weak partial correlations (~0.02–0.03), making cross-study comparison imperfect."}

{"outcome":"DIRECT_SUB_OPTIMAL","best_model_id":"PGS000054","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"All five candidates are direct matches on concept alignment (trait_efo = late-onset Alzheimer's disease). Endpoint fidelity is strongest for PGS000053/PGS000054/PGS000334/PGS004918 because their phenotyping_reported is explicitly late-onset Alzheimer’s disease (familial LOAD for PGS000053/PGS000054; LOAD for PGS000334/PGS004918). PGS002289 is less endpoint-faithful for the target because its phenotyping_reported is a cognition/age-interaction phenotype rather than Alzheimer’s disease status, despite the trait label.

Among the endpoint-faithful set, PGS000054 provides the clearest PRS-discrimination signal via a strong per-SD effect size (OR=1.73, 95% CI 1.57–1.93) with simple covariates (age, sex), which domain guidance treats as a strong indicator and more informative than full-model AUROC. PGS000053 shows only moderate OR evidence (OR=1.29), and PGS000334 reports an R²=0.191 from a C+T model with unknown covariates, which domain guidance flags as potentially non-comparable/suspect for a complex trait when covariates are unclear; PGS004918 reports only full-model AUROC (0.731) without PRS-only metrics and with small validation (n=136), so its AUROC cannot be used as a PRS-only discriminator.

The main limitation is that none of the candidates provides clearly PRS-only AUC/R² in a comparable way (and several key fields like covariates are unknown), so the choice relies primarily on effect-size evidence and endpoint coherence, lowering confidence to moderate and making the overall direct-match recommendation sub-optimal rather than high-quality."}
